# ── vault stores are not the site's to carry ──────────────────────────
# Until v0.2.76 this folder was also an sgit vault and git tracked its
# encrypted store (.sg_vault/bare/) as a zero-knowledge mirror. The mirror
# had no reader and was 91% of the repository, so it was retired and
# purged from history at v0.2.84 — see /case-studies/one-tree-two-remotes.html.
# Any vault cloned into this tree now stays out of git entirely.
.sg_vault/

# the board vault, cloned in place: its encrypted store and its own credential tier are not
# the site's to carry. The cards (issues/*.md) ARE tracked — they are the build's input.
admin/content/team/issues/.sg_vault/

# ── local credential tier ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Write keys of published demo vaults (admin/local/demo-keys/<name>-vault-key), the
# board vault's push token, anything else plaintext. NEVER commit. The validator reads
# each key from here at build time and fails if one appears in a tracked file.
admin/local/

# defence in depth: no unwrapped key material anywhere, ever
*.pem

# Git's own metadata (sgit honours .gitignore, so this also keeps git
# internals out of any vault snapshot taken of this tree).
.git/

# Build/OS noise.
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
